//! HTTP client backed by the browser Fetch API.
//!
//! Requests require the `Http` and `Net(host:port)` capabilities. A URL host
//! must be an ASCII host name or a full IP address, such as `127.0.0.1`; other
//! hosts fail with kind `"parse"`. The browser controls forbidden request
//! headers, omits ambient cookies (`credentials: "omit"`), and enforces CORS
//! rules on cross-origin responses. Redirects are not followed and fail with
//! kind `"http"`. The browser buffers the full response body before `open`
//! returns, so `max_http_body` applies to `open` as well as `request`, and
//! `timeout` covers the entire exchange.

import io
import json
